"""Primary-source evaluation of forum discovery leads; no forum text copied."""
DATE='2026-10-28'
RESEARCH=[
 ('S48','Public AnandTech graphics research discussion','https://forums.anandtech.com/threads/exciting-new-features-research-advancements-in-gaming-graphics-adjacent-software.2633516/','Discovery only. Browser read page1; web reader inspected selected passages on pages2–7. Browser showed8 pages while cached reader showed7; page8 could not be fetched. Coverage is incomplete, not an exhaustive thread review.','discussion / discovery',''),
 ('S49','ReSTIR PT Enhanced','https://research.nvidia.com/labs/rtr/publication/lin2026restirptenhanced/','Primary abstract: reciprocal neighbor selection, footprint-aware reconnection and duplication maps; reported2–3x versus the paper’s ReSTIR PT baseline. Full125.96MB PDF exceeded reader limit; no full-paper evaluation claimed.','research abstract','2026-05'),
 ('S50','Real-Time Level-of-Detail Rendering with ReSTIR','https://research.nvidia.com/labs/rtr/publication/wang2026levelOfDetail/wang2026levelOfDetail.pdf','Paper §§4–6: partial bijective surface mapping through consistent UVs supports temporal reuse when topology changes. Mapping is needed at primary and reconnection vertices. Unmapped/distorted UVs unsupported or degraded; implementation uses one LOD per object per frame, not per-ray LOD.','research paper','2026-07'),
 ('S51','Multi-Layer Reservoir Splatting','https://research.nvidia.com/labs/rtr/publication/hong2026multilayer/','Primary abstract: multiple screen-space layers preserve previously occluded histories; depth ranges reduce extra ray queries and active domains limit maintenance. Incremental cost remains. Full97.8MB PDF exceeded reader limit.','research abstract','2026-07'),
 ('S52','Compatibility-Guided Neighbor Selection','https://research.nvidia.com/labs/rtr/publication/junkins2026compatibility/','Primary abstract reports6–29% lower SMAPE and22–49% lower temporal covariance for2–5% incremental cost in its tests. RTXDI3.1 already lists compatibility-guided selection; inspect the pinned implementation before duplicating work.','research abstract','2026-07'),
 ('S53','Variable Rate Tracing ReSTIR GI','https://mateuszkolodziejczyk00.github.io/2025/06/18/variable-rate-tracing-restir-gi.html','Author implementation report: ray budgets depend on materials, variance and history. San Miguel RT-reflection pipeline5.82ms versus9.42ms, tracing/shading1.23 versus4.74ms, with similar denoising costs. LaptopRTX4090,1080p internal/4K DLSS output. Missing shadows, grazing specular detail and self-reinforcing under-sampling are documented.','author implementation report','2025-06-18'),
 ('S54','Many-Light Rendering Using ReSTIR-Sampled Shadow Maps','https://research.nvidia.com/labs/rtr/publication/zhang2025many-light/','Primary abstract: ReSTIR chooses lights for full-resolution shadow maps; other lights use imperfect low-resolution maps. Raster many-light alternative with approximate visibility, not full PT or a shadow-error-free RT substitute.','research abstract','2025-05'),
 ('S55','ReSTIR Path Guiding','https://research.nvidia.com/labs/rtr/publication/zeng2025restirpg/','Paper pp7–8: fit directional mixtures from accepted paths into a spatial hash grid; combine guiding with BSDF sampling. Paper reports about102.8MB recorded path information per bounce at1080p plus152bytes per valid grid cell. Glossy quality and overhead remain material.','research paper','2025-12'),
 ('S56','Neural Two-Level Monte Carlo Real-Time Rendering','https://arxiv.org/html/2412.04634v1','Cache estimates are corrected by a path-traced residual integral; omitting residuals is a different biased mode. §7 discusses complex occlusion, glossy detail and unstable/slow dynamic training. CUDA/Falcor results do not establish Vulkan or DX12LinAlg compatibility.','research paper','2024-12-05'),
 ('S57','NIRC implementation licensing','https://github.com/Mishok43/IVD_NIRC/tree/097364d154de114492e530b713b8e272dca762b7','Pinned README assigns code GPLv3 unless stated otherwise, documents CC-BY4; linked rootLICENSE absent in inspected listing. Falcor4.4/tiny-cuda-nn dependencies have separate terms. Do not import into MIT core; paper study and independent implementation remain possible.','license / code inspection','2026-01-20'),
 ('S58','Real-Time GPU Tree Generation','https://gpuopen.com/download/Real-Time_GPU_Tree_Generation.pdf','HPG2025 paper p7:51KiB persistent parameters is not total VRAM.1.5GiB WorkGraph backing memory;34.8GiB is a theoretical baked highest-detail comparison.3.13ms generation+G-buffer and7.74ms full scene on7900XTX1080p. Ray-traced vegetation integration is future work.','research paper','2025'),
 ('S59','GPU tree minimal sample license','https://github.com/Bloodwyn/gptree/blob/adf96a5b989eb01d0881e50dd2003cd2ad22276e/LICENSE','MIT minimal sample atadf96a5b989eb01d0881e50dd2003cd2ad22276e. Simplified paper subset requiring D3D12WorkGraphs1.1 MeshNodes; WorkGraphPlayground dependency483706a038ed6d668550076817e3b782905890ec also has MIT-style terms. Audit bundled SDKs/assets separately.','license / code inspection','2025-06-21'),
 ('S60','MiniDXNN v0.4.0 neural texture compression','https://gpuopen.com/learn/minidxnn-v040-interactive-neural-texture-compression/','AMD example targets SM6.10/D3D12LinAlg with preview Agility1.721 and DXC1.10.2605.4. Has headless training/input-encoding examples and C++ fallback; GUI path is GPU-only. This does not provide a Vulkan/Slang drop-in or prove material compression quality.','vendor implementation documentation','2026-08-13'),
 ('S61','Ubisoft neural texture compression lead','https://www.ubisoft.com/en-us/news/ignt.58488/shipping-neural-texture-compression-in-assassin-s-creed-mirage','Reader retrieved title and placeholder ellipses only. Detailed implementation, shipping status and licensing could not be established; do not infer them from the title or forum.','access-limited primary page',''),
 ('S62','MiniDXNN pinned MIT license and notices','https://github.com/GPUOpen-LibrariesAndSDKs/MiniDXNN/blob/8d1899f17d364b5e8a3756e72965c5e9e0d466ea/LICENSE','MIT root license at8d1899f17d364b5e8a3756e72965c5e9e0d466ea. NOTICE.md separately lists dependency and Pexels image terms. Software-LinAlg/no-include switches suggest a porting opportunity, not verified Slang/SPIR-V support. Article’s amdadvtech clone URL returns404; use this repository.','license / code inspection','2026-07-10'),
 ('S63','DXC disables Work Graphs for SM6.10','https://github.com/microsoft/DirectXShaderCompiler/pull/8798','Merged August31; links DXIL spec PR918. Scoped SM6.10/DXIL1.10 exclusion means LinAlg and Work Graphs must not be assumed to share one shader target. This does not remove released Work Graphs from older supported targets.','compiler change','2026-08-31'),
 ('S64','Advanced Shader Delivery developer workflow','https://developer.microsoft.com/en-us/games/articles/2026/09/prepare-your-game-for-advanced-shader-delivery-asd/','Microsoft describes SODB packaging and Xbox PC app delivery. Candidate D3D12 distribution workflow; not a Vulkan feature or proof every shader/PSO hitch disappears.','vendor distribution documentation','2026-09-15'),
 ('S65','Basix repeated-device and in-flight lifetime receipt','https://github.com/BasixMaster/Basix_Engine/blob/main/docs/lifecycle-results.json','Seven-case local validation harness:3devices×3cycles,36864 pointer pixels,73728 rays,76500 texture comparisons,189 contract rejections including27 truly pending retirements;27 foreign-registry checks. Clean whole-process validation logs; no SDK, device-loss or multiqueue claim.','local measured correctness','2026-10-28'),
 ('S66','Basix hidden-window resize receipt','https://github.com/BasixMaster/Basix_Engine/blob/main/docs/window-results.json','Four processes:8presents at actual resized client extents,3empty0x0 acquisitions and restoration; controlled failure cleanup passed. Supported UNORM format used after initial sRGB/storage validation failure. Window stays hidden; no displayed-pixel, actual OS minimize or device-loss claim.','local measured correctness','2026-10-28'),
 ('S67','Streamline custom ProjectID initialization','https://github.com/NVIDIA-RTX/Streamline/blob/625db07d4bca5abc67d781c42af7e7fb0761f1b6/source/plugins/sl.common/commonEntry.cpp','Pinned code chooses NGX ProjectID initialization when projectId and engineVersion are nonempty, including custom engines. Stable GUID/version is an available evaluation path; absence of an NVIDIA-issued application ID is not by itself a demonstrated local blocker. Runtime evaluation remains pending.','code inspection','2026-10-28'),
]

def apply(sections,sources,source,section,table,cite):
 for sid,title,url,notes,kind,date in RESEARCH:
  source(sid,title,url,notes,kind=kind,date=date)
  s=sources[-1]
  s['quality']='Primary research or implementation evidence; author results are not Basix measurements.'
  if sid in ('S49','S51','S52','S54'):s['access']='abstract';s['limitations']='Abstract-level evaluation only; detailed integration and cost remain unverified.'
  if sid=='S48':s['quality']='Discovery context only; incomplete page coverage.';s['access']='partial'
  if sid=='S61':s['access']='limited';s['quality']='Title only; no technical conclusion.'
  if sid=='S50':s['rights']='Paper states CC-BY4.0; linked with original summary, no implementation code adopted.'
  if sid=='S55':s['rights']='Author PDF says personal use, not redistribution. Link/original summary only; no reusable code license established.'
  if sid=='S57':s['rights']='README GPLv3 code claim plus missing linked LICENSE inconsistency. No source imported into MIT core.'
  if sid=='S59':s['rights']='MIT at pinned revision; retain notices and independently audit dependencies before adoption. Reference only.'
 by={s['id']:s for s in sections}
 by['implementation-status']['body']=by['implementation-status']['body'].replace('M1 overall and broader lifecycle are partial; actual SDK evaluation, window/device-failure handling, shared materials, full PT, streaming, GPU cages and DXR2 remain open.','M1 overall remains partial; repeated-device/in-flight lifecycle passes. Hidden-window resize/restoration passes, while actual SDK evaluation, OS minimize/device-loss handling, shared materials, full PT, streaming, GPU cages and DXR2 remain open.')
 by['implementation-status']['body']+='<p><strong>New lifecycle acceptance:</strong> three actual device sessions pass the seven-case harness, including real pending-retirement rejection and exception cleanup while queued work is held. Hidden Win32 resize/restoration passes four processes. <a href="lifecycle-results.json">Lifecycle receipt</a> · <a href="window-results.json">window receipt</a>. Both are local correctness checks.</p>'+cite('S65','S66')
 by['dlss']['body']+='<p><strong>Next actual SDK gate:</strong> use a stable custom-engine ProjectID GUID and engine version, signed compatible Streamline SR modules, and explicit pre-device Vulkan requirements. Query support and provide color/depth/motion/output image state, then test evaluation and engine binding restoration. The documented ProjectID path must be tried before treating a missing NVIDIA-issued application ID as a blocker. No SDK has yet run in Basix.</p>'+cite('S67','S19')
 by['research-map']['body']+='<p><strong>Q9 · High:</strong> which discussion leads improve Basix without invalidating temporal reuse or the MIT boundary? Prioritize surface correspondence, sampling quality and total memory. Stop at independently testable adoption gates; retain abstract-only and authenticated-access gaps.</p>'
 by['summary']['body']+='<p><strong>New research:</strong> prioritize LOD/history correspondence before extra geometry density, then test compatibility-guided reuse and adaptive ray budgets. Procedural vegetation, path guiding and neural texture/cache work stay separate optional branches. <a href="#research-update">Read the evaluated forum leads</a>.</p>'
 by['dx-roadmap']['body']+='<p><strong>Compiler-target correction:</strong> DXC’s merged SM6.10 change disables Work Graphs for that target. Track LinAlg and Work Graphs as separately compiled/capability-gated paths; do not infer older released Work Graphs support was removed.</p>'+cite('S63')
 by['lessons']['body']+='<p><strong>New lesson:</strong> geometric detail and temporal sampling must share stable surface provenance. More triangles can reduce reuse efficiency; lower ray counts can miss detail; tiny procedural assets can require large scratch allocations. Measure total-frame quality, latency and peak memory before promotion.</p>'+cite('S50','S53','S58')
 section('research-update','Research update: sampling, detail and procedural worlds', '''
<p class="lead">Useful discussion leads become experiments with explicit baselines. None of these new techniques is implemented or benchmarked in Basix.</p>
<p><strong>Access and freshness:</strong> public thread passages from pages1–7 were reviewed selectively. Browser pagination showed8 pages while cached web pages showed7; page8 was inaccessible. A second user-supplied authenticated conversation could not be read. No private conversation text or identifiers are included. Primary sources below determine technical conclusions; forum predictions about RDNA5, consoles or DX13 do not establish capabilities.</p>'''+cite('S48')+'''
<h3>First priority: preserve detail through temporal reuse</h3>'''+table(['Candidate / priority','Evidence and fit','Basix adoption test'],[
 ('LOD-aware ReSTIR · high','UV-based correspondence supports reuse across topology changes. Requires consistent UVs; current paper implementation uses one LOD per object per frame. Not a proven match for arbitrary per-cluster/per-ray LOD. '+cite('S50'),'Extend asset provenance to surface mappings. Test primary and reconnection vertices, overlapping/missing UVs, streaming eviction and animated transitions; reject invalid histories.'),
 ('Compatibility-guided neighbors · high after DI','Choose spatial candidates by geometric compatibility. Paper reports an added cost; inspect existing RTXDI3.1 support before a new implementation. '+cite('S52','S17'),'Compare uniform and guided selection with identical seeds/budget; measure error and temporal correlation on thin geometry and depth edges.'),
 ('Multi-layer splatting · medium','Preserve occluded histories across screen-space layers. Evidence here is the primary abstract; extra storage and maintenance remain. '+cite('S51'),'Expose layer count/history byte limits. Test reveal/re-occlude loops, topology changes and stale surfaces; compare equal time and peak VRAM.'),
 ('ReSTIR PT Enhanced · high research, later implementation','Reciprocal neighbors, safer reconnection and decorrelation. Reported2–3x is relative to its ReSTIR PT baseline; full paper was not fetched. '+cite('S49'),'Start after reference PT/reuse. Isolate each change against the same scene and estimator; include energy/colour convergence, rare paths and dynamic lights.'),
 ('Variable rate tracing · high after temporal baseline','Author reports lower reflection cost, with missing shadows and difficult glossy/disoccluded regions. Not hardware VRS, nor guaranteed lossless sampling. '+cite('S53'),'Provide full-rate reference and a minimum discovery budget; evaluate grazing highlights, small lights and motion. Time allocation/reuse/denoise as well as tracing.'),
 ('ReSTIR-selected shadow maps · fallback','Raster alternative selects some lights for detailed maps and approximates remaining visibility. '+cite('S54'),'Compare matched many-light scenes to hardware RT shadows with declared map-memory, update latency and shadow-error budgets.')])+'''
<h3>Second priority: memory and optional indirect lighting</h3>'''+table(['Candidate','What is viable','Required boundary'],[
 ('Procedural vegetation','Compact deterministic grammars can reduce persistent asset data; the paper still allocates1.5GiB backing memory. Its RT integration is future work. MIT minimal sample exists. '+cite('S58','S59'),'Compute/mesh-shader baseline first. Stable seeds, connectivity and previous/current positions; separately budget generated geometry, BLAS/TLAS and scratch. Cages help only where topology contracts remain valid.'),
 ('ReSTIR Path Guiding','Fit directional distributions from reused paths to improve next-frame candidates. Recorded-path memory scales with bounces; keep BSDF fallback. '+cite('S55'),'Compare equal-time error and total memory, normalized PDFs/MIS, glossy paths and moving lights. No source license established for copying an implementation.'),
 ('Neural incident-radiance cache with residual','Two-level estimator corrects approximate cache output with a traced residual; cache-only mode has different bias. '+cite('S56'),'Reference PT convergence and dynamic recovery first. Inspected implementation declares GPLv3: do not import into MIT core. Independent implementation and dependency audit required. '+cite('S57')),
 ('Neural material compression / LinAlg','MiniDXNN offers a concrete DX12 preview research tool, including a C++ fallback. Pinned code is MIT; assets/dependencies retain separate terms. Vulkan inference/training must be a separate adapter. '+cite('S60','S62'),'First compare scalar/FMA GPU inference to the CPU reference. Keep conventional BCn/residency baseline; measure channel errors, mip/filter/anisotropy, cooking and occupancy. Software-LinAlg switches alone do not prove a Slang port.'),
 ('Ubisoft NTC / future UE reference renderer','Ubisoft body was inaccessible; forum commentary about future UE reference paths was not independently verified. '+cite('S61'),'Retain as leads; no shipping, speed or license claim and no dependency in the current roadmap.')])+'''
<div class="callout"><strong>Proposed dependency flow</strong><p>Reference materials/PT → valid motion and surface correspondence → DI/reuse baseline → one sampling improvement at a time → optional guiding/cache. In parallel: resident meshlets → LOD mapping → cluster/cage comparison → procedural vegetation integration.</p></div>
<p><strong>Do not multiply reported speedups.</strong> Reuse, guiding, adaptive budgets and reconstruction compete for the same work and memory. Record full-frame timings, equal-time image/temporal error, VRAM/scratch, input/output resolution and rendered versus generated frames. Compare against the same scene, materials, ray/bounce budget and driver. Preserve unsupported-feature fallbacks.</p>
<p><strong>Separate deployment lead:</strong> Advanced Shader Delivery deserves investigation when a D3D12 distribution path exists. It concerns packaged shader data and delivery; ordinary Vulkan pipeline-cache/warm-up engineering remains necessary.</p>'''+cite('S64')+'''
<p>Roadmap entries below remain pending or deferred until their acceptance tests run. A completed literature review never marks engine implementation complete. New research priorities augment M3/G1 and the optional R subgates; current M1 interoperability work remains the immediate implementation prerequisite.</p>
<p class="doc-caption">Research changelog ·28Oct2026: evaluated selected public discussion leads against primary papers/code; retained inaccessible/abstract-only gaps; added sampling, procedural vegetation and neural-compression adoption gates.</p>''')

def enrich_library(library):
 library['summary']=['Initial CPU/GPU foundation and scoped lifecycle/window tests have local correctness evidence; advanced rendering ideas are separately labeled proposals or author reports.']
 library['questions'].append(dict(id='Q9',title='Forum leads with viable engine adoption gates',topic='rendering',priority='high',status='partial',why='Improve detail and lighting without importing incompatible code or assuming additive speedups.',depends_on=['Q1','Q3','Q4'],search_terms=['LOD ReSTIR','variable rate tracing','procedural trees','neural texture compression'],source_types=['primary paper','author implementation','license'],evaluation='Separate full paper, abstract, discovery and inaccessible evidence; test applicability to NoGraphicsAPI.',stop_when='Selected candidates have independent acceptance gates and explicit coverage gaps.',coverage='Selected public pages1–7 and primary leads covered; page8/authenticated discussion and two large PDFs not available in full.'))
 for fid,title,claim,ids in [
  ('F10','Surface mapping precedes temporal LOD reuse','Topology-changing LOD needs explicit surface correspondence; the inspected LOD paper assumes consistent UVs and does not demonstrate per-ray LOD.',['S50']),
  ('F11','Sampling improvements require isolated comparisons','Compatibility selection, splatting and adaptive tracing affect different reuse costs and quality. Published speedups cannot be multiplied into an engine forecast.',['S49','S51','S52','S53']),
  ('F12','Procedural parameters are not total GPU memory','The tree paper’s compact parameter size excludes a large WorkGraph backing allocation, and RT vegetation remains future work.',['S58','S59']),
  ('F13','Neural research needs estimator and license boundaries','Residual correction matters for unbiased cache estimates; the inspected NIRC implementation declares GPLv3 and is not an MIT-core dependency.',['S56','S57']),
  ('F14','Guiding and neural texture work remain optional','Guiding has per-bounce storage cost; MiniDXNN is a DX12 preview research tool, not a verified Vulkan adapter.',['S55','S60'])]:
  library['findings'].append(dict(id=fid,title=title,question_ids=['Q9'],topic='rendering',claim=claim,evidence_type='analytical',confidence='medium',context='Primary-source update '+DATE+'; no new Basix runtime results.',strengths='Explicit mechanisms, baselines, rights and acceptance gates.',limitations='Selected/abstract-level coverage where stated; no cross-vendor or end-to-end performance verification.',implications='Preserve M1 first; add independent later roadmap experiments.',tags=['ReSTIR','LOD','procedural','neural','roadmap'],evidence=[dict(source_id=s,locator='Source notes and linked primary methods/limitations',relation='supports',note='Supports bounded reported mechanism, not Basix performance.') for s in ids]))
 library['findings'].append(dict(id='F15',title='Scoped lifecycle and hidden-window checks passed',question_ids=['Q2'],topic='rendering',claim='Three real device sessions and held asynchronous texture submissions pass local oracles; hidden-window resizing/zero-size restoration and controlled cleanup pass. Actual SDK/device-loss remain open.',evidence_type='measured',confidence='high',context=DATE+' Windows/RTX4090/NVIDIA617.42 with pinned core/SyncVal layer.',strengths='Actual incomplete timeline values, identical-metadata registry isolation, complete process log scans and bounded failures.',limitations='One adapter; hidden clear-only presentation; no actual OS minimize, visible-pixel oracle, multiqueue or device-loss recovery.',implications='Complete only M1b-lifecycle; resize/recovery and overall M1 remain partial.',tags=['validation','lifecycle','window'],evidence=[dict(source_id=s,locator='Receipt cases/runs and GPU fields',relation='supports',note='Local bounded correctness only.') for s in ['S65','S66']]))
 library['scope_changes'].append('User supplied two discussions. Added selected public leads and primary verification; authenticated discussion/page8 remained inaccessible. No private content published.')
 library['search_log'].append(dict(date=DATE,phase='update',engine='Public forum discovery then primary papers/vendor/author code',query='ReSTIR LOD PT Enhanced splatting variable rate guiding procedural trees MiniDXNN',source_ids=[r[0] for r in RESEARCH],outcome='Independent adoption gates added; incomplete thread/full-paper/access coverage recorded.'))
